!
! How far two shares an / ad and bn / bd are from one whole, in Trebago
! (heirloom_rules.h HR1), cross-multiplied over ad * bd:
! bn * ad - (ad - an) * bd, which is an * bd + bn * ad - ad * bd; 0 exactly
! when the two make one whole. Trebago is exact to 64 bits: a denominator
! of 0 or below divides by zero (ok is 0), refused, as Sutra refuses it;
! a negative part, a share past its whole or a part past nine digits is
! answered here and refused by Sutra: held.
trebago gap
  in  an(n), ad(n), bn(n), bd(n)
  out gap(n)
  var ok(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, ad(i))) * min(1, max(0, bd(i)))
  gap(i) = (bn(i) * ad(i) - (ad(i) - an(i)) * bd(i)) / ok(i)
end
